---
/** The school's pattern book, rendered once per page (from Header) so every
    inline SVG can paint with url(#gm-chintz). Original vector work: a chintz
    repeat of cabbage roses, buds, forget-me-not sprigs and loose leaves, packed
    onto a 200px tile at three sizes and as many angles, so no row or column
    ever lines up into a visible grid. Inked through the --c-* tokens, which is
    how one drawing serves both the day parlour and the lacquered room. Not
    display:none: a pattern in an undisplayed SVG does not paint.

    Aged prints (B1 item 7): the inks are 20% lower in chroma (theme.css), each
    motif is printed twice, a plain fill pass a hair off true and a second
    pass laid over it with a thin brown outline (the misregistration of an old
    block print), there are three rose variants, and the ground carries a
    static grain. The tile block below is written by
    scripts/themes/grandmillennial/build-patterns.mjs, which also writes the
    big papered-wall and toile files in assets/ (external, so the browser
    caches them and no page carries them inline). Edit the motifs here; run
    the script to redo the tile and the walls. */
---
